// @test regression/INV140-varip-and-array-udt-fields
// @description A PRE-EXISTING false positive, found while wiring imported UDT surfaces: `scanTypeFieldAtCurrent` dropped any field it could not shape-match, and a dropped field name then reads as a typo ("Object has no field b"). It missed `varip`-qualified fields (`varip float b`) because `varip` is a KEYWORD but not a type token, and UDT-typed array fields (`bucket[] c`) because only the keyword branch suffix-scanned `[]`. TV accepts all of these (probed 2026-07-15); `varip` is the ONLY legal field qualifier, `var` being CE10288. This cost the vendored robbatt/lib_profile/44 its poc/vah/val fields (13 captured of 30). See investigations/INV140-imported-udt-surfaces/notes.md.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects errors: 0
//@version=6
indicator("x")
type bucket
    float v
type t
    int a
    varip float b
    bucket[] c
    varip float[] d
o = t.new()
plot(o.a + o.b + array.size(o.c) + array.size(o.d))
